<p>Mandan's first municipal airport was Eielson Field, south of the eastern end of the area now commonly called the Strip. Although the airport was formally dedicated May 2, 1933, construction continued that July as workers cleared and stacked timber from the site. The City reserved the wood as home-heating fuel for the following winter in place of coal.</p>

